# Fork-owned SSoT trio (see docs/designs/t3-company-os-ssot.md): prefer OUR
# side when a selective upstream cherry-pick/merge touches these files.
# Convenience, not a guarantee — the driver must be defined once per clone
# (`git config merge.ours.driver true`; .gitattributes alone cannot ship it)
# and it only fires on both-sides-changed merges. The real protection is
# `pnpm check:ssot-guards` (scripts/check-ssot-guards.mjs) in CI.
/roadmap.md merge=ours
/backlog.md merge=ours
/design.md merge=ours

# Markdown test fixtures are compared byte for byte against what a renderer emits, and
# every renderer here emits LF. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default,
# and what this repo's owner has set) writes them back as CRLF on the next checkout and
# the byte-for-byte assertion fails on Windows while Linux CI stays green — see PC-002
# AC5 and server/src/__tests__/issue-dossier-fixture.test.ts.
#
# Deliberately narrow in BOTH directions. A repo-wide `*.md text eol=lf` would renormalize
# the SSoT trio above; a directory-wide `fixtures/** text eol=lf` would set `text` on every
# file under fixtures/ and so turn OFF git's binary auto-detection there — the first .png
# or .pdf fixture added later would have its 0x0d 0x0a byte pairs rewritten on checkout and
# be silently corrupt. Scoping to *.md keeps auto-detection for everything else.
server/src/__tests__/fixtures/*.md text eol=lf
